346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (A profile of Mrs Karuna Bhoojedhur-Obeegadoo, Mauritius' first fully qualified female actuary)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (It is 4:30pm on a Wednesday afternoon. Over coffee at Paul in So'Flo, the conversation unfolds at its own unhurried pace - the kind that only happens when someone genuinely enjoys where they are and who they are with. The woman across the table has just returned from Ottawa, her schedule packed with board meetings and international travel. Yet she says, without a trace of obligation, that it is always a pleasure to meet the new generation of actuaries.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (It does not take long to realise something else. She loves to talk. And we are more than happy to listen.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Mrs Karuna Bhoojedhur-Obeegadoo is Mauritius' first fully qualified female actuary, former Group CEO and Chairperson of SICOM, and former board member of MCB Group Ltd, current board member of MCB Equity Fund Ltd and GuardRisk.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 93 0 R
/Pg 19 0 R
/A [701 0 R 0]
/K [5]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Mrs Karuna B Obeegadoo's story begins at Queen Elizabeth College, where she completed her HSC as a laureate. She was drawn to mathematics and physics - and pursued exactly that at A-level, alongside economics. It was a relative who casually suggested actuarial science. She looked it up. LSE offered it. A path was set.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (There, she also had the opportunity to be in the one of the first ever batches to take up Introduction to Computer Science and learning the ones and zeros.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (After graduating, she returned to Mauritius and joined SICOM as a clerical officer. The actuarial field in the country was, at the time, barely a handful of people. But she was not going to let that be the end of the story.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (FROM LAUREATE TO LONDON)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (A CEO AT 34)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (After a few years in London, she returned to SICOM. Not long after, an unexpected opportunity came her way - the CEO position. She was thirty-four. A young mother. And a woman.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (She hesitated. Then she said yes.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (It was 1996. She would go on to lead SICOM, retiring as Group CEO in October 2017 after nearly 30 years with the company. Along the way, she earned recognition that stretched well beyond the island: )
/Pg 20 0 R
