/E (She began studying for her actuarial exams largely on her own, without structured support or a clear roadmap. The exams were unforgiving. She recalls the first time she failed one - a significant shock. But she reflects on it without bitterness. "Failing forms you," she says. "It shows you that you are not invincible - that you can fall, and that you must get back up." Resilience, she says, is the key chain. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E ("It was very tough," she says. Not once, but twice in the same breath, as if the memory still carries weight. A chance encounter in the corridors of SICOM changed everything: a representative from Swiss Re encouraged her to join their London office. She took the leap.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
