/P 96 0 R
/E (She never had a single long-term mentor - no one figure who guided her from start to finish. Instead, she assembled herself from fragments. "Each person gave me a piece," she says. "A direction, a method, a moment of clarity. Those fragments came together to make who I am." It is, she suggests, perhaps a more honest account of how most people actually develop.)
/Pg 22 0 R
